34,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems our reporting process is more cumbersome than I feared, especially regarding assets that require outside appraisals. We need to be careful about adding complexity to our quarter-end.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I've found that our capacity for oversight is uneven; our software board seats are full, while our logistics experts are underutilized. We should consider the human cost of our next move.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"My findings suggest that our most successful exits were in back-office financial tools, and that customers in certain sectors are far more loyal during price increases than others.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"Our reserves are being depleted faster than planned, and our current credit line is quite restrictive regarding what it actually accepts as security. We must consider our long-term liquidity.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"I've noticed a significant disparity in deployment speeds. Security reviews for certain sectors take much longer, and hardware-dependent delivery has proven far more volatile than pure software.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Misaki, if our credit line is restrictive, does that mean we should prioritize companies with assets that are easier to leverage, or perhaps those that require less follow-on capital?","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"I suspect the latter. If our board seats for software are already saturated, adding another software-heavy holding might strain our time as much as it strains our capital.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"That is a very thoughtful point, Jonathan. I wonder if we should look for a balance between the stability of the customer base and the operational burden we can actually handle.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Mizuki, exactly. We need assets that provide real security for borrowing, as our current credit line doesn't value subscription contracts. We cannot afford another holding that drains reserves without offering collateral.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, if software is saturated and hardware is volatile, we are in a tight spot. However, the volatility I saw was specific to custom assembly, not necessarily all physical assets.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"If we want to avoid the appraisal delays I found, we should probably steer clear of anything with depots or installed hardware, regardless of the collateral value.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"That would certainly simplify our reporting, but we must weigh that against the fact that our logistics advisers are currently sitting idle.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"It is a delicate balance, but perhaps we can find a path that utilizes our available expertise without overwhelming our reporting capacity.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"If we avoid hardware to save on appraisals, we might be sacrificing the only assets our credit line actually values. We need to be very strategic about this trade-off.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, we should also consider that the security review time for certain sectors is nearly triple that of others. If we go for software, we must ensure it isn't in a highly regulated field.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,It seems we are caught between a need for collateral and a need for operational simplicity. We must be very cautious about the specific industry we enter.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. We need a candidate that doesn't overstretch our board capacity or our recruiters' ability to find specialized staff, while still fitting our financial constraints.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I believe we should prioritize a company that demonstrates strong customer loyalty, as that provides a different kind of stability that can offset some of these operational risks.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I agree with Shizue, but only if that loyalty translates into a business model that doesn't bleed our reserves dry before we can reach a sustainable exit.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,"We have a clear set of constraints now: avoid high-security review sectors, be mindful of hardware volatility, and consider our current board saturation. Let's see which candidates actually fit these criteria.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
