59,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"We have four candidates: Clinic Scheduler, Ledger Bridge, Fabric Loop, and Harvest Sensor. Given my concerns about appraisal delays, I am immediately wary of Fabric Loop and Harvest Sensor.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Looking at the staffing side, Fabric Loop and Harvest Sensor would utilize our idle logistics experts, but Ledger Bridge and Clinic Scheduler would further saturate our software board seats.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I recall that back-office financial tools have been our most successful exits, which makes Ledger Bridge very appealing, and I'm curious about the loyalty of the medical clinics for Clinic Scheduler.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"If we need collateral for our credit line, Fabric Loop and Harvest Sensor are the only ones with physical assets, but the reserve drain makes me lean toward the leaner model of Ledger Bridge.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Mizuki, @Shizue, Clinic Scheduler likely falls into that high-security review category I mentioned, which would delay deployment. Ledger Bridge seems the safest bet for a quick, clean start.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shion, I agree. Ledger Bridge avoids the appraisal nightmare of depots and sensors, and it doesn't seem to carry the regulatory baggage of medical records.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"While it adds to our software board load, the staffing for a financial tool is far more manageable than finding field crews for the other options.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,I agree. Ledger Bridge aligns with our history of successful exits in financial tooling and avoids the risks we've discussed.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"It is the most prudent choice. It avoids the collateral issues of the others while minimizing the risk of an early, unplanned call on our reserves.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"It seems we are in rare agreement. Ledger Bridge avoids the deployment delays of medical software and the volatility of hardware, making it the most logical choice.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,I am satisfied with this conclusion. I vote for Ledger Bridge.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I agree with the consensus. I vote for Ledger Bridge.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I believe it is the most stable path forward. I vote for Ledger Bridge.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I agree. I vote for Ledger Bridge.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,It is the most efficient and least risky option. I vote for Ledger Bridge.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
